/*:
 * @plugindesc v1.4.0 [EN] - Custom enemy animation: sprite sheet OR individual PNG. State & Skill animations supported.
 * @author Anaryx Plugin
 * @url https://anaryx-plugin.itch.io/
 *
 * @help
 * ============================================================================
 * AG Enemy Animator Core v1.4.0 - Documentation (English)
 * Author  : Anaryx Plugin
 * Website : https://anaryx-plugin.itch.io
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Replaces the default RPG Maker MV enemy motion system with a custom
 * frame-based animation system. Supports TWO animation modes:
 *
 *   MODE 1 - SPRITE SHEET  : frames arranged horizontally in one image
 *   MODE 2 - INDIVIDUAL PNG: separate PNG files per frame
 *
 * Both modes can be mixed freely within the same notetag.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * HOW TO FIND STATE ID / SKILL ID IN RPG MAKER MV
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * STATE ID:
 *   Open Database → States → see the number in the leftmost column (ID).
 *   Default RPG Maker MV states:
 *     ID 1  = KO (Dead)
 *     ID 4  = Poison
 *     ID 5  = Blind
 *     ID 6  = Sleep
 *     ID 7  = Paralysis
 *     ID 8  = Rage
 *     ID 9  = Confusion
 *     ID 10 = Charm
 *     ID 11 = Silence
 *     ID 12 = Slow
 *     ID 13 = Stop
 *
 * SKILL ID:
 *   Open Database → Skills → see the ID number in the leftmost column.
 *   Example: Skill "Fire" = ID 45, so write skill_45
 *
 * AUTO STATE (state from enemy trait/passive):
 *   Open Database → Enemies → tab "Traits" → Add Trait → "State" → Auto State
 *   States assigned here are automatically active when battle starts.
 *   This plugin detects auto-states the same way as regular states,
 *   so state_N animation will be active from the start of battle.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * BASIC NOTETAG - SPRITE SHEET MODE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Place the sprite sheet in /img/enemies/ with the same name as the enemy battler.
 * Frames are arranged HORIZONTALLY left to right, equal width.
 * Frame width = total image width / number of frames
 * Frame index starts at 0.
 *
 *   <AG_EnemyAnim>
 *   idle: 0-3 loop speed:5
 *   attack: 4-7 speed:4
 *   hit: 8-10 speed:6
 *   death: 11-15 speed:8
 *   </AG_EnemyAnim>
 *
 * Parameters:
 *   idle/attack/hit/death  - Animation type (required)
 *   0-3                    - Frame range: start-end (required, use N-N for 1 frame)
 *   loop                   - Add this flag to make the animation loop
 *   speed:N                - Ticks per frame advance (lower = faster)
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * NOTETAG - INDIVIDUAL PNG MODE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *   <AG_EnemyAnim>
 *   idle: img:actor1_1,actor1_2,actor1_3 loop speed:5
 *   attack: img:actor1_4,actor1_5,actor1_6,actor1_7 speed:4
 *   hit: img:actor1_8,actor1_9,actor1_10 speed:6
 *   death: img:actor1_11,actor1_12,actor1_13 speed:8
 *   </AG_EnemyAnim>
 *
 * PNG files are loaded from /img/enemies/ (no .png extension needed).
 * You can also use range shorthand with ~ :
 *   img:actor1_1~actor1_3  = actor1_1, actor1_2, actor1_3
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * STATE ANIMATIONS - ANIMATION WHEN AFFECTED BY STATUS (Poison, Sleep, etc.)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Format: state_<ID>: <animation definition>
 *
 * Example (Poison = ID 4, Sleep = ID 6):
 *
 *   <AG_EnemyAnim>
 *   idle: 0-1 loop speed:5
 *   state_4: 6-7 loop speed:3
 *   state_6: 8-8 loop speed:8
 *   state_7: 8-8 loop speed:10
 *   attack: 2-4 speed:4
 *   hit: 5-5 speed:6
 *   death: 9-9 speed:8
 *   </AG_EnemyAnim>
 *
 * State animation rules:
 *   - Active only during idle (does not interrupt attack/hit/death)
 *   - If enemy has multiple states, the HIGHEST state ID wins
 *   - When state expires, automatically returns to normal idle
 *   - AUTO STATE (from enemy traits) is detected automatically from battle start
 *
 * How to assign Auto State in RPG Maker MV:
 *   Database → Enemies → select enemy → Features tab
 *   → Add Feature → State → States → select desired state
 *   The state_N animation will be active from the start of battle.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * SKILL ANIMATIONS - DIFFERENT ANIMATION PER SKILL
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Format: skill_<ID>: <animation definition>
 *
 * Use this when an enemy has multiple skills with different animations.
 * Example: normal attack uses frames 2-4, special skill "Fire" (ID 45) uses 10-13
 *
 *   <AG_EnemyAnim>
 *   idle: 0-1 loop speed:5
 *   attack: 2-4 speed:4
 *   skill_45: 10-13 speed:3
 *   skill_46: img:boss_special1,boss_special2,boss_special3 speed:3
 *   hit: 5-5 speed:6
 *   death: 9-9 speed:8
 *   </AG_EnemyAnim>
 *
 * How to find Skill ID:
 *   Database → Skills → see the ID number in the left column.
 *
 * How to assign skill to enemy:
 *   Database → Enemies → tab "Action Patterns" → Add → select skill.
 *
 * Skill animation rules:
 *   - skill_N has the same priority as attack (3)
 *   - If a skill has no custom animation, falls back to the attack animation
 *   - After finishing, automatically returns to idle/state
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * MIXING SPRITE SHEET + PNG MODES
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *   <AG_EnemyAnim>
 *   idle: img:actor1_1,actor1_2,actor1_3 loop speed:5
 *   attack: 4-7 speed:4
 *   skill_45: img:boss_fire1,boss_fire2 speed:3
 *   state_4: img:actor1_poison1,actor1_poison2 loop speed:4
 *   hit: img:actor1_8,actor1_9,actor1_10 speed:6
 *   death: 11-15 speed:8
 *   </AG_EnemyAnim>
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * DISPLAY SIZE (optional)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *   size: 128x192       → absolute pixel size
 *   size: 50%x75%       → percentage of original bitmap size
 *   size: 50%           → uniform scale (same percentage for width and height)
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * HUE SHIFT (optional)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *   hue: 180    → 0 = no change, 360 = full rotation
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * ATTACK ZOOM TWEEN (optional)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *   attackzoom: scale:1.4 offsety:60 duration:12
 *
 *   scale:N    → zoom multiplier at peak (default: 1.3)
 *   offsety:N  → downward offset at peak in pixels (default: 40)
 *   duration:N → tween duration in frames (default: 10)
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * ANIMATION PRIORITY
 * ============================================================================
 *   death (5) > hit (4) > attack/skill (3) > state_N (2) > idle (1)
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * FULL EXAMPLE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *   <AG_EnemyAnim>
 *   size: 200x300
 *   hue: 0
 *   attackzoom: scale:1.3 offsety:40 duration:10
 *   idle: 0-1 loop speed:6
 *   attack: 2-4 speed:4
 *   skill_45: 10-13 speed:3
 *   skill_46: img:boss_special1,boss_special2 speed:3
 *   state_4: 6-7 loop speed:3
 *   state_6: 8-8 loop speed:8
 *   hit: 5-5 speed:6
 *   death: 9-9 speed:8
 *   </AG_EnemyAnim>
 *
 * ============================================================================
 */
